The '''''Gozanti''-class cruiser''', also known as the '''''Gozanti''-class armed transport''', '''''Gozanti''-class shuttle''' or '''''Gozanti''-class vessel''', was a class of [[armor]]ed [[starship]] used by various factions, and as such had many modified sub-variants, including the [[Black Sun frigate]], the [[Imperial Gozanti-class cruiser|Imperial ''Gozanti''-class cruiser]], the [[C-ROC Gozanti-class light cruiser|C-ROC ''Gozanti''-class light cruiser]], the [[IGV-55 surveillance vessel]], and the [[Gozanti-class Assault Carrier|''Gozanti''-class Assault Carrier]]. During the [[First Order-Resistance War]], the [[Gozanti Armed Transport]] shared a similar name. During the [[Galactic Civil War]] Imperial Gozanti-class cruiser was typically seen commanded by a [[Lieutenant]].

==Characteristics==
[[File:C-ROC_Cruiser_SWX.png|thumb|left|250px|The C-ROC ''Gozanti''-class light cruiser, one of the many models produced over the years]]
The ''Gozanti''-class [[cruiser]] was a [[starship]] that could act as a [[freighter]] and cruiser. It could be modified to accommodate a twin [[laser turret]] in a dorsal mount and a heavy [[laser cannon]] on its ventral side. The Gozanti also had a loading elevator on the bottom near the nose and docking ports to the side near the cockpit section.<ref name="Fire Across the Galaxy">{{Rebels|Fire Across the Galaxy}}</ref> The ships had a [[hyperdrive]] and three [[engine]]s.<ref name="Rebels Guide" />

Over the years since it's introduction, there were numerous variants of ''Gozanti''-class cruisers produced. The most famous version,<ref name="SW:HC 20" /> was the [[Imperial Gozanti-class cruiser|Imperial ''Gozanti''-class cruiser]]. Furthermore, the Galactic Empire would iterate upon the standard [[Imperial Gozanti-class cruiser|Imperial ''Gozanti''-class cruiser]],<ref name="TIE Manual" /> employing variations that included the [[Gozanti-class Assault Carrier|''Gozanti''-class Assault Carrier]],<ref name="Gozanti Armada" /> an alternative configuration, and a heavily modified model, being the [[IGV-55 surveillance vessel]].<ref name="ESOV" /> The [[C-ROC Gozanti-class light cruiser]] was a modified version that was designed to hold more cargo space. It was commonly used by criminal organizations,<ref name="SW:HC 20" /> however also served in the [[Imperial Navy]]. The [[Separatist Gozanti-class cruiser|Separatist ''Gozanti''-class cruiser]] was a modified ''Gozanti'' used by the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist Alliance]] for their own purposes. The [[Black Sun]] cartel used [[Black Sun frigate]], a modified ''Gozanti'' for their criminal activities.<ref name="TIE Manual" />

==History==
===Twilight of the Republic===
[[File:Gozanti_cruiser-TPM.png|left|250px|thumb|A ''Gozanti''-class cruiser in Mos Espa]]
''Gozanti''-class cruisers were introduced by the [[Corellian Engineering Corporation]]<ref name="Rebels Guide" /> around [[34 BBY]],<ref name="Introduced" /> and they proved to be one of the major starship success stories of the late [[Republic Era]].<ref name="SW:HC 20" />

Shortly before [[Anakin Skywalker]] won the [[Boonta Eve Classic]], a ''Gozanti''-class cruiser with red markings was seen in the [[spaceport]] of [[Mos Espa]] on [[Tatooine]].<ref name="TPM">{{Film|I}}</ref>

At some point prior to the Clone Wars, a ''Gozanti''-class cruiser crashed into the canyons on the planet [[Balnab]]. The surviving crew were pit droids that used the ship to create a large hologram of [[Albee Dewaw]]. They used the hologram to rule over the [[Balnab (group)|Balnab]] denizens near the crashed cruiser.<ref name="Nomad Droids">{{TCW|Nomad Droids}}</ref>

===The Clone Wars===
During the Clone Wars, the cruiser was adopted by various factions, including the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]]. At least three were in the fleet led by the [[ST-series military strategic analysis and tactics droid|super tactical droid]] [[Aut-O]].<ref name="TCW:SW">{{TCW|Secret Weapons}}</ref> One cruiser was on Zygerria as [[Dooku]] arrived to discuss the [[Death penalty|execution]] of Anakin Skywalker with [[Miraj Scintel]].<ref name="Escape from Kadavo" />

[[File:GOZANTICLASSCRUISERONZYGERRIA.jpg|thumb|left|250px|A ''Gozanti''-class cruiser on [[Zygerria]] during the [[Clone Wars]]]]
After the [[Battle of Patitite Pattuna]], [[C-3PO]] and [[R2-D2]] arrived on the planet Balnab and discovered that the Balnab denizens were being ruled by [[DUM-series pit droid|pit droids]] using the control room of a ''Gozanti''-class cruiser. R2-D2 showed this to them, so they destroyed the control room, which caused the cruiser to explode.<ref name="Nomad Droids" />

The [[Black Sun]] crime syndicate also used modified ''Gozanti''-class cruisers. They were forced into joining [[Maul|Darth Maul's]] [[Shadow Collective]] and took part in the [[Takeover of Mandalore|takeover]] of [[Mandalore]].<ref name="TCW:Shades">{{TCW|Shades of Reason}}</ref> Several joined with Maul's forces after the [[battle of Zanbar]]. These ships were painted black with gold highlights, including a stylized rim of a [[star]] placed over the cruiser's front, taken from the syndicate's emblem.<ref name="Son of Dathomir">[[Darth Maul — Son of Dathomir 2|''Darth Maul — Son of Dathomir'' 2]]</ref>

While using a malfunctioning [[Joben T-85 speeder bike]], [[Force-Sensitive Outcast|former]] [[Jedi]] [[Padawan]] [[Ahsoka Tano]] nearly collided with a ''Gozanti'' in an [[underworld portal]], but she regained control of the [[speeder]] in time.<ref name="Gone with a Trace">{{TCW|Gone with a Trace}}</ref>

===Imperial Era===
[[File:Gozanti-Naboo.png|thumb|right|250px|A ''Gozanti''-class Assault Carrier dropping in two All Terrain Armored Transports during the Battle of Theed]]
The [[Imperial Gozanti-class cruiser|Imperial ''Gozanti''-class cruiser]],<ref name="TIE Manual" /> and the alternative configuration of that design, the [[Gozanti-class Assault Carrier|''Gozanti''-class Assault Carrier]].<ref name="Databank Assault Carrier">{{Databank|imperial-assault-carrier|Imperial Assault Carrier}}</ref> The [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[Advanced Science Division]] made use of these vessels, including [[Unidentified Imperial Gozanti-class cruiser (Balmorra)|one]] utilised early in the [[Imperial Era]],<ref name="Tipping Point">{{TBB|Tipping Point}}</ref> Imperial Gozanti-class Cruisers would go on to be utilized throughout the [[Galactic Civil War]]. The cruiser on several occasions carried TIE fighters, such as during the [[Mission to Hosnian Prime]] in [[4 ABY]],<ref name="Squadrons">''[[Star Wars: Squadrons]]''</ref> while the Assault Carrier sub-variant often dropped [[All Terrain Armored Transport]]s into battle, such as during the [[Battle of Hoth]] in [[3 ABY]] and the [[Battle of Theed]] in 4 ABY.<ref name="Battlefront II">''[[Star Wars Battlefront II]]''</ref>

===New Republic Era===
[[File:NiteOwlsGozanti.png|thumb|200px|left|Bo-Katan and three other Mandalorians hijacking an Imperial remnant ''Gozanti'' ship]]
During the [[New Republic Era]], various [[Imperial Remnants]], such as [[Moff]] [[Gideon]]'s continued to utilize ''Gozanti'' craft. In [[9 ABY]], an Assault Carrier leaving [[Trask]] was [[Assault on the Imperial Gozanti freighter|boarded]] by [[Mandalorian]]s led by [[Bo-Katan Kryze]], who wanted the craft to help in her effort to [[Conflict on Mandalore|retake]] the [[planet]] [[Mandalore]] from the Empire. The Mandalorians fought the Imperials onboard and successfully hijacked the ship.<ref name="The Heiress" />

===The First Order===
[[File:FirstOrderSympathizer-HSCK.png|thumb|right|200px|First Order sympathizers piloting an old Imperial ''Gozanti''-class cruiser]]
Old ''Gozanti'' craft continued to be utilized into the [[Cold War]] and the [[First Order-Resistance War]] by the [[First Order]] and their sympathizers, who piloted the ships while patrolling.<ref name="SWZ">{{FFGXW2|set=Huge Ship Conversion Kit|cardname=First Order Sympathizers}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
The ''Gozanti''-class cruiser first appeared in [[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace|''Star Wars'': Episode I ''The Phantom Menace'']].<ref name="Episode I">{{Film|I}}</ref>

